Q: Google Mock - how do I return a different value using EXPECT_CALL to exit a loop A: <p>There is a simple solution to your problem. Create an instance of InSequence before your expectations. This will guarantee that the written expectations are called in the same order. </p>

<pre><code>InSequence s;
EXPECT_CALL(mock, Read(address)).Times(4).WillRepeatedly(Return(1));
EXPECT_CALL(mock, Read(address)).Times(1).WillOnce(Return(0));
</code></pre>

<p>Furher Informations: <a href="https://github.com/google/googletest/blob/master/googlemock/docs/CookBook.md#expecting-ordered-calls" rel="nofollow noreferrer">click</a></p>

Q: bootstrap modal pop up on dropdown select A: <p>You can try this....</p>

<pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
    &lt;head&gt;
      &lt;title&gt;Bootstrap Example&lt;/title&gt;
      &lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;
      &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"&gt;
      &lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="http://maxcdn.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/3.3.5/css/bootstrap.min.css"&gt;
      &lt;script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/1.11.3/jquery.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
      &lt;script src="http://maxcdn.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/3.3.5/js/bootstrap.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
    &lt;/head&gt;
    &lt;body&gt;
        &lt;div class="container"&gt;
          &lt;h2&gt;Basic Modal Example&lt;/h2&gt;
          &lt;!-- Trigger the modal with a button --&gt;
                &lt;select&gt; 
                    &lt;option&gt; List 1 &lt;/otion&gt;
                    &lt;option&gt; list 2&lt;/option&gt;
                    &lt;option&gt; List 3&lt;/option&gt;
                    &lt;option  data-toggle="modal" data-target="#myModal"&gt; Click For Modal &lt;/option&gt;
                &lt;/select&gt;
          &lt;!-- Modal --&gt;
              &lt;div class="modal fade" id="myModal" role="dialog"&gt;
                &lt;div class="modal-dialog"&gt;      
                  &lt;!-- Modal content--&gt;
                  &lt;div class="modal-content"&gt;
                        &lt;div class="modal-header"&gt;
                          &lt;button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal"&gt;&amp;times;&lt;/button&gt;
                          &lt;h4 class="modal-title"&gt;Modal Header&lt;/h4&gt;
                        &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;div class="modal-body"&gt;
                          &lt;p&gt;Some text in the modal.&lt;/p&gt;
                        &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;div class="modal-footer"&gt;
                          &lt;button type="button" class="btn btn-default" data-dismiss="modal"&gt;Close&lt;/button&gt;
                        &lt;/div&gt;
                  &lt;/div&gt;          
                &lt;/div&gt;
              &lt;/div&gt;  
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/body&gt;
